.TH DVBIPITOOLS 1 "2026-08-27" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dvbipitools \- multicall binary bundling every dvbipitools tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dvbipitools
\fItool\fR [\fIargs\fR ...]
.br
.B dipi
\fIshort\-name\fR [\fIargs\fR ...]
.br
\fItool\fR [\fIargs\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dvbipitools
is one executable containing every tool in this project
(\fBdipibcg\fR, \fBdipibim\fR, \fBdipicam378\fR, \fBdipidescramble\fR,
\fBdipifccret\fR, \fBdipimetrics\fR, \fBdipiradiohead\fR, \fBdipirec\fR,
\fBdipirist\fR, \fBdipiscan\fR, \fBdipisds\fR, \fBdipisrt\fR,
\fBdipitvhead\fR, \fBdipixmltv\fR, \fBdipixy\fR), reached one of three ways:
.TP
.B by full tool name
\fBdvbipitools\fR \fItool\fR [\fIargs\fR ...], e.g. \fBdvbipitools dipiscan \-h\fR.
.TP
.B by short name
\fBdipi\fR \fIshort\-name\fR [\fIargs\fR ...], where \fIshort\-name\fR drops
the \fBdipi\fR prefix, e.g. \fBdipi scan \-h\fR. Both entry points accept
either the full or the short name.
.TP
.B by symlink or hardlink
Linking \fBdvbipitools\fR under any tool's own name (e.g.
.I dipiscan
\-> \fBdvbipitools\fR) makes running that link behave exactly like the
standalone tool, with \fIargs\fR passed through unchanged.
.PP
Run
.B dvbipitools
or
.B dipi
with no arguments for the full applet list. Once dispatched, a tool's own
options, exit status, and behavior are identical to running it standalone;
see that tool's own manual page.
.B dvbipitools
itself adds no options of its own.
.PP
Not all 15 tools are necessarily present: \fBdipicam378\fR and
\fBdipidescramble\fR require OpenSSL, \fBdipirist\fR requires librist,
\fBdipisrt\fR requires libsrt, each built in only if that dependency was
found (matching the standalone build).
.SH APPLETS
Full name and short name (for the
.B dipi
entry point):
.PP
.RS
dipibcg          bcg
.br
dipibim          bim
.br
dipicam378       cam378
.br
dipidescramble   descramble
.br
dipifccret       fccret
.br
dipimetrics      metrics
.br
dipiradiohead    radiohead
.br
dipirec          rec
.br
dipirist         rist
.br
dipiscan         scan
.br
dipisds          sds
.br
dipisrt          srt
.br
dipitvhead       tvhead
.br
dipixmltv        xmltv
.br
dipixy           xy
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dvbipitools dipiscan \-m 239.19.75.0 >hd.m3u
Run \fBdipiscan\fR by its full name.
.TP
.B dipi scan \-m 239.19.75.0 >hd.m3u
Same, via the short form.
.TP
.B ln \-s dvbipitools dipirec && ./dipirec \-i ... \-o ...
Run \fBdipirec\fR via a symlink to \fBdvbipitools\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or bare invocation with no arguments (applet list printed).
.TP
.B 2
Unrecognized applet name or subcommand.
.TP
.B other
Whatever the dispatched tool itself returns.
